 "capsule": "The 'State of Kuwait' here denotes the fully sovereign nation-state that emerged on 19 June 1961, when Kuwait's 1899 protectorate treaty with Britain was annulled by mutual agreement and Sheikh Abdullah Al-Salim Al-Sabah proclaimed independence, prompting a brief Iraqi territorial claim deterred by British and later Arab League troop deployments. Flush with oil revenue, Kuwait built an extensive welfare state, founded Kuwait University (1966), channeled budget surpluses through the world's first sovereign wealth fund (originating in the 1953 Kuwait Investment Board and reorganized as the Kuwait Investment Authority in 1982), and held its first National Assembly elections in 1963 under a 1962 constitution. This 'golden era' of independent statehood ended abruptly on 2 August 1990, when Iraqi forces under Saddam Hussein invaded and briefly annexed the country, an occupation reversed only by the U.S.-led coalition in the 1991 Gulf War.",
